{
  "Ezekiel.1.25.8-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.12.11, number: 1 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezekiel 1:25.8</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezekiel 1:25.8</h1>\n  <h2>Add dagesh and rafe to dalet. Add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/images/2022.12.11/1-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    The dalet has both a dagesh and a rafe; a contradiction.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    BHL has no dagesh in the dalet.\n                    BHL Appendix A has both a dagesh and a rafe on the dalet.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes.xml?2022.12.11-1\">2023.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2022.12.11-1</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezekiel.14.14.8-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 32 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezekiel 14:14.8</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezekiel 14:14.8</h1>\n  <h2>Remove unsupported dagesh in yod of qere word. Add note 'q'. [דָּנִיֵּ֣אל]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/32-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere word in the left margin, דניאל, has a yod between the nun and the alef.  The tsere and munah appear at the start of the alef in the ketiv body text for this yod. No support for a dagesh in the yod is present, however. Note: In the book of Daniel, the letters of the ketiv word for Daniel include the yod, i.e. Dan 1:6.5.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh, tsere, and munah on the yod in the qere form, דָּנִיֵּ֣אל.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-32\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-32</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezekiel.14.20.3-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 33 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezekiel 14:20.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezekiel 14:20.3</h1>\n  <h2>Remove unsupported dagesh in yod of qere word. Add note 'q'. [דָּנִיֵּ֣אל]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/33-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere word in the left margin, דניאל, has a yod between the nun and the alef. The tsere and munah appear under the alef in the ketiv body text for this yod. No support for a dagesh in the yod is present, however. Note: In the book of Daniel, the letters of the ketiv word for Daniel include the yod, i.e. Dan 1:6.5.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh, tsere, and munah on the yod in the qere form, דָּנִיֵּ֣אל. BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-33\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-33</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezekiel.16.36.10-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.12.11, number: 10 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezekiel 16:36.10</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezekiel 16:36.10</h1>\n  <h2>Change first consonant from bet to kaf. Add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/images/2022.12.11/10-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    The text is in poor condition. \n                    The scribe doesn't always distinguish the bet and kaf carefully.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The BHL has a bet as the first letter.\n                    BHL Appendix A makes no comment on this verse.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    Breuer has a kaf as the first letter.\n                 </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes.xml?2022.12.11-10\">2023.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2022.12.11-10</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezekiel.28.16.2-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.12.11, number: 22 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezekiel 28:16.2</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezekiel 28:16.2</h1>\n  <h2>Add dagesh to kaf. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/images/2022.12.11/22-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    The putative dagesh is well-sized, a little out of position, and brown.\n                    Note the rafe above the kaf, however.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The BHL has no dagesh in the kaf.\n                    BHL Appendix A has a dagesh in the kaf.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes.xml?2022.12.11-22\">2023.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2022.12.11-22</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezekiel.28.3.5-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 34 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezekiel 28:3.5</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezekiel 28:3.5</h1>\n  <h2>Remove unsupported dagesh in yod of qere word. Add note 'q'. [מִדָּֽנִיֵּ֑אל]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/34-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere word in the left margin, מדניאל, has a yod between the nun and the alef. The tsere and etnachta appear under the alef in the ketiv body text for this yod. No support for a dagesh in the yod is present, however. Note: In the book of Daniel, the letters of the ketiv word for Daniel include the yod, i.e. Dan 1:6.5.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh, tsere, and etnachta on the yod in the qere form, מִדָּֽנִיֵּ֑אל. BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-34\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-34</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezekiel.34.12.21-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.12.11, number: 25 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezekiel 34:12.21</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezekiel 34:12.21</h1>\n  <h2>Possible merkha under nun, add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/images/2022.12.11/25-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    The near-vertical line under the first nun has a slight northeast-to-southeast inclination.\n                    This inclination isn't as great as that in the preceding word where the accent is clearly a tipeha.\n                    It's probably a meteg or merkha, but must be transcribed as a tipeha.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The BHL has a merkha under the first nun.\n                    BHL Appendix A makes no comment on this verse.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes.xml?2022.12.11-25\">2023.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2022.12.11-25</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezekiel.46.12.12-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2021.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2021.08.07, number: 22 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezekiel 46:12.12</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezekiel 46:12.12</h1>\n  <h2>Word lacks accent, add note 'c'; MAM ends the word with a Maqaf (  ס־  ).</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/images/2021.08.07/22-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Ben Denckla</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes.xml?2021.08.07-22\">2021.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2021.08.07-22</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezekiel.48.15.6-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.12.11, number: 34 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezekiel 48:15.6</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezekiel 48:15.6</h1>\n  <h2>Remove qadma from nun, add pashta to yod. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/images/2022.12.11/34-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    The pashta/qadma accent is clearly on the yod.\n                    Pashtas occur more frequently on the final letter of a word than qadmas.\n                    Ben Denckla offers a cantillation rule: \n                        \"When a qadma/pashta appears on a letter that closes a syllable and ends a word\n                             ... it should be interpreted as a pashta\".\n                    Given the uncertainty and need to transcribe the accent,\n                       the accent is transcribed here as a pashta with a 't' added.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The BHL has a pashta/qadma over the nun; \n                        it's hard to tell the difference even in this modern, printed document.\n                    BHL Appendix A makes no comment on this verse.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes.xml?2022.12.11-34\">2023.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2022.12.11-34</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>"
}
